 ],
 "level_notes": {
  "1": "ISO/IEC 13568:2002 defines syntax, type system and semantics; it is one of ISO's publicly available standards (free zip download). Before that, Spivey's Z Reference Manual (ZRM, 2nd ed. 1992), now freely distributed by the author, was the de-facto standard and is still the dialect most tools and textbooks use. Section links point into the ZRM PDF served from the author's GitHub repository via jsDelivr (#page=N is the PDF page).",
  "0": "There is no reference implementation: fuzz (Spivey; type checker for the ZRM dialect, C) and the Community Z Tools (CZT; Java, parser/type checker/animator for ISO Z and Object-Z) are the main open implementations. Z is usually written as LaTeX markup (zed/fuzz style files) or in Unicode/ZML."
 },
